Discovery coordination — Aster Grove Makerspace

@sd-researcher — Liam: confirm that all ten allowed evidence records are explicitly synthetic-labelled, checking only: librarian-01, patron-02, teen-patron-03, ops-log-2026, front-desk-04, facilities-05, accessibility-lead-06, program-lead-07, annual-review, board-brief. Report provenance status and cite the exact record IDs; do not add or rewrite evidence.

@sd-mapper — Kai: review the persisted current journey and identify its failure-demand moments, using only the same ten evidence IDs. Report journey step, failure-demand signal, and evidence ID(s); do not invent quotes or metrics and do not promote the journey.

Coordination plan: run provenance verification and failure-demand mapping in parallel; reconcile their typed handoffs against the existing discovery artifacts; then present Mehran with a discovery gate report. I will stop before Define and await Mehran’s framing decision.

Unresolved questions for Mehran: (1) which framing question should govern Define after these two checks, and (2) whether any provenance exception or failure-demand gap should be treated as a discovery blocker.

Define phase opened under owner receipt ag-gate-001 (idempotency key astergrove-gate-discover-01); the provenance caveat is accepted and Kai’s four candidate moments are the approved input set.

@sd-librarian — Nadia: before any Define artifact dispatch, verify the project’s registered method catalog with sd_method_list. Return the available Define-compatible method IDs/manifests, their required input kinds, reviewGate, machine-checkable acceptance rules, and dependency order. Use the authoritative ASD store; do not create or mutate artifacts. The approved framing question is: “How might the makerspace make every member’s first independent making session succeed without repeated staff explanation?”

Orchestration hold: I will dispatch Define methods only after the registry/dependency check. No phase gate is being advanced by this message.

Define dispatch — registry-verified, evidence-root methods

@sd-synthesizer — Elena: run the registered `affinity-diagramming` method against the authoritative 10-record evidence set for project aster-grove-makerspace-6a8498ef. Frame the analysis against: “How might the makerspace make every member’s first independent making session succeed without repeated staff explanation?” Produce the typed `insight-set` only through the ASD store; do not mutate source evidence or promote the artifact. Acceptance contract: at least 4 nodes, at least 2 evidence refs per node, non-empty `theme`; traceability and provenance required. Use only the registered evidence IDs.

@sd-ideator — Rowan: run the registered `jobs-to-be-done` method against the same authoritative 10-record evidence set and framing question. Produce the typed `insight-set` only through the ASD store; do not mutate source evidence or promote the artifact. Acceptance contract: at least 2 nodes, at least 1 evidence ref per node, non-empty `insight`; no “feature request”, “app”, or “button” language; traceability and provenance required. Use only the registered evidence IDs.

Orchestration: these two evidence-root methods may run in parallel. After their store writes, I will route at least one valid insight-set through the Critic; behavioural-personas and opportunity-matrix remain blocked until a critic-passed insight-set exists. No Define gate advance is requested.
